"We are arrived."

First spoken Lojban ((And)) ever heard:

((And)) (answering phone): Hello?
((Nick Nicholas|Nick)): ''mi vizykla''
And: (thinks: ''What the fuck??'')

----
The story as told by And sooner after it occurred, in a discussion of ((the Glasgow Conversation)):

''When Nick phoned me up when he arrived the first thing he said was {i vizykla} and I thought he was speaking Klingon - the last syllable was (Was Footnote: klah), and I wasn't expecting {i}, and hands up everyone who doesn't know the rafsi for {vi}.''

So it looks like the comment has morphed over the years. Nick, any recollection?

Nope, although it sounds like the kind of thing I'd do. I remember it being dark, and I'm pretty sure that's all the Lojban I uttered...
